{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791128495,"nonce":"x21BsdSwyzNKfaaNIgfcHfq6CeA=","message":"Letter spacing in measurement: done (Blinc deeeec98, ashui 53663b6). ashui installs FontTextMeasurer, which measures through TextLayoutEngine::layout and counts the spacing after every character, as drawing does.\n\nLeft here: subpixel positioning, the cause of the 1px residual on centred labels (AlignScene toggle-b, outline). Blinc bd5ff7ba adds TextRenderer::prepare_text_subpixel: pass Some(SubpixelX { phases: NonZeroU8::new(3), origin_x }), with origin_x the run's x on the device, draw at origin_x.floor(), and the fraction is baked into the raster. Only for runs nothing rotates or skews. It costs about 2.8x atlas entries at 3 phases, falling back to phase 0 above 75% atlas use. ashui prepares text in blinc_abi/src/text.rs with prepare_text_with_style.\n\nAtlas: upload only what changed — Blinc has dirty rects. For an atlas GC (Blinc cf07ff40), count epochs in text walks, not frames. ashui's glyph rects are in atlas pixels, divided by textureSize when sampled, so growth keeps them valid.","files":null}]}